# HTTP / API

Follow the app's existing controller style (invokable, resource, or Action class). Do not introduce a second pattern.

Keep controllers thin: authorize, validate, call application code, return a response. Put multi-step writes in a service/action **only if the app already uses that layer**.

**Do:** FormRequest (or the app's existing validator) for request input; Policy/Gate or FormRequest `authorize()` for protected actions; Eloquent API Resources when the app already uses them.

**Don't:** validate only in the controller when siblings use FormRequest; authorize only in the UI; return raw models with hidden credentials; call `env()` here; load unbounded relations on the request path.

```php
// Don't — untrusted input + no authorize
public function update(Request $request, Post $post)
{
    $post->update($request->all());
}

// Do — match FormRequest + policy already in the app
public function update(UpdatePostRequest $request, Post $post)
{
    $this->authorize('update', $post);
    $post->update($request->validated());
    return PostResource::make($post);
}
```

Do not change database schema from this layer unless the task requires it (then follow `52-eloquent.mdc`).

## Fullstack contract

When UI is in-repo, trace: form → FormRequest → controller → model/job → resource/JSON → UI states (loading/error/empty/permission). Do not duplicate business rules in the frontend.
